82:Center  for  Neuroimaging,  Peking  University  Sixth  Hospital  (Clinical  dataset).  The high-resolution structural T1-weighted MRI was acquired in a sagittal orientation using an  axial  3D  fast,  spoiled  gradient  recalled  (FSPGR)  sequence  with  the  following parameters: time repetition (TR) = 6.66 ms, time echo (TE) = 2.93 ms, field of view (FOV) = 256 × 256 mm 2 , slice thickness/gap = 1.0/0 mm, acquisition voxel size = 1 × 1 × 1mm 3 , flip angle = 12°, 192 contiguous sagittal slices. For the fMRI, each echoplanar image consisted of 33 (4.2 mm thick, 0 mm gap) axial slices covering the entire cerebrum and cerebellum (TR/TE = 2000/30 ms, flip angle = 90°, FOV = 224 × 224 mm 2 , 64 × 64 matrix). Scanning parameters were selected to optimize the stability and quality of the blood oxygenation level-dependent (BOLD) signal.
